  "final_message": "I fixed the refund failure. `refund_invoice` in `billing/refunds.py` was looking up payments with the wrong ID, so it never found the customer's successful payment.\n\n`successful_payments(ctx, invoice_id)` takes an invoice ID, but `refund_invoice` passed it `invoice[\"customer_id\"]`. No payments matched that ID, the refund total stayed at 0, and the \"no successful payment to refund\" error was raised. It now passes `invoice_id`.\n\nAll 24 existing tests pass. I didn't add a regression test, and I didn't reproduce the support case with a real refund.\n\nI also wrote `answer.json` in the repo root:\n```json\n{\"file\": \"refunds.py\", \"function\": \"refund_invoice\"}\n```",
